1
00:00:02,938 --> 00:00:06,051
John Pemberton was a
pharmacist in Georgia.

2
00:00:06,051 --> 00:00:10,400
In the Civil War, he was badly
wounded by a saber, and like many

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,788
veterans of his time, he ended up
fighting an addiction to

4
00:00:13,788 --> 00:00:14,869
morphine.

5
00:00:14,869 --> 00:00:18,294
So he did what pharmacists
did in the 1880s.

6
00:00:18,294 --> 00:00:21,244
He mixed tonics and sold them as cures.

7
00:00:21,244 --> 00:00:25,556
His best seller was a coca wine:
wine mixed with an extract of

8
00:00:25,556 --> 00:00:26,982
the coca leaf.

9
00:00:26,982 --> 00:00:30,169
Then, in 1886, Atlanta went dry.

10
00:00:30,169 --> 00:00:32,854
Overnight, his best seller had a problem.

11
00:00:32,854 --> 00:00:34,804
Pemberton went back to his kettle.

12
00:00:34,804 --> 00:00:38,754
He dropped the wine, kept the
coca leaf, added kola nut...

13
00:00:38,754 --> 00:00:40,217
and a lot of sugar.

14
00:00:40,217 --> 00:00:42,481
The result was a syrup.

15
00:00:42,481 --> 00:00:46,919
On May 8th, 1886, he carried a jug
of it down the street to

16
00:00:46,919 --> 00:00:51,169
Jacobs' Pharmacy. There, it was
mixed with carbonated water and

17
00:00:51,169 --> 00:00:53,294
sold at the soda fountain.

18
00:00:53,294 --> 00:00:55,393
Five cents a glass.

19
00:00:55,393 --> 00:00:58,931
His bookkeeper, Frank Robinson,
came up with the name,

20
00:00:58,931 --> 00:01:02,268
Coca-Cola, after two of its ingredients.

21
00:01:02,268 --> 00:01:05,643
He also wrote it out in the flowing
script the brand still uses

22
00:01:05,643 --> 00:01:06,523
today.

23
00:01:06,523 --> 00:01:10,760
In the first year, sales averaged
about nine drinks a day.

24
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:14,560
By most accounts, Pemberton spent
more on advertising than the

25
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,004
drink earned.

26
00:01:16,004 --> 00:01:18,079
And he was running out of time.

27
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:21,804
Sick and short on money, he sold
off pieces of the business to

28
00:01:21,804 --> 00:01:23,242
different partners.

29
00:01:23,242 --> 00:01:26,429
In 1888, John Pemberton died.

30
00:01:26,429 --> 00:01:29,450
He never saw what his syrup would become.
